  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing sustainable landscape management in UNESCO sites in the Hispanic Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing biodiversity, ecosystem (including coastal and marine) and geodiversity in UNESCO sites is a priority for SIDS in the Caribbean to address environmental and anthropocentric risks, including extreme weather events, biodiversity loss, critical Earth system changes, and natural resource shortages. UNESCO will leverage its scientific expertise, global, regional and local networks (Iberomab, Youth, MAB Island and Coastal Marine Network, Geolac, Multi Designated International Sites), to drive impactful actions that strengthen resilience against these escalating threats. Advancing policy advice, science, local and Indigenous knowledge for biodiversity, ecosystems, and geodiversity conservation in UNESCO designated sites for sustainable management and landscape connectivity.</narrative>
  </description>
